# bench: active/crafter-recipes.case run for 20000 ticks
# Crafters craft their grid when powered and each slot loses one item; the result and any crafting remainder go one by one into a crafter in front, whose comparator (read by wire) counts its filled slots, or in bulk into a hopper.
# Recipes: shaped (3x3, a mirrored one, a 2x2 trimmed out of the grid with a tag ingredient), shapeless (three items in any slots, a single item with a remainder), transmute (dyeing a shulker box), and two dyes mixing ahead of the special recipes, and the special recipes whose results keep default components (two fresh tools repair into one, four bricks make a plain pot).
# A shulker box dyed its own color, a grid without a recipe, a honey bottle with a stick, paper with a firework star, a lone arrow, two empty maps, two book and quills and the emptied shears grid powered again craft nothing.
# The iron block that went into the first lane's crafter crafts back into ingots, which go in bulk into the chest in front.
tmc-case 2
size 15 3 19
key
  s = minecraft:stone
  c = minecraft:chest[facing=south,type=single,waterlogged=false]
  Q = minecraft:crafter[crafting=false,orientation=north_up,triggered=false]
  h = minecraft:hopper[enabled=true,facing=down]
  k = minecraft:comparator[facing=west,mode=compare,powered=false]
